# Keep the build context small and reproducible: never copy build outputs, the git history, or IDE state into the
# image build (the publish rebuilds from source inside the SDK stage).
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/.vs/
.git/
.github/
**/*.user
artifacts/
TestResults/
**/.sqlflow/
# The Rust workspace's build output (gigabytes once built locally); images rebuild from source.
tools/target/
**/node_modules/
docs/
# The MCP image embeds the indexed corpora (manifest, reference pages, key census, and the internals
# wiki) at compile time; they are the parts of docs/ that belong in the context (see Dockerfile.mcp).
!docs/reference/
!docs/wiki/
*.md
# The GUI builds in its own image (gui/Dockerfile with the gui/ context); keep its trees out of the .NET context.
gui/node_modules/
gui/dist/
gui/e2e/
gui/playwright-report/
gui/test-results/
gui/.tsbuild/

# Trees no image needs, kept out of the context because EVERY root-context build (control plane, worker, MCP)
# tars the whole repository before the daemon applies these rules: 534 MB of upload and scan per build, for
# files no Dockerfile reads. Excluding them is what keeps a build submitting in seconds rather than minutes.
data/
